    title: "taint return lift: a source call written directly in a Go multi-value return (return os.Getenv(x), nil) has no recorded result position, so a caller's blank target still seeds err and the error chain climbs (WI-sitaf sibling)"  # 7f15
    status: todo_hard  # 7f15
    priority: 3  # 7f15
    parent:  # 7f15
    tags:  # 7f15
    - taint  # 7f15
    - analysis_quality  # 7f15
    - adr_0017  # 7f15
    isbefore: []  # 7f15
    duplicate_of: []  # 7f15
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 7f15
    pr_ref:  # 7f15
    description: "FOUND 2026-11-04 while draining INV-komoj (dev 4c9d5d4d2f; record ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/komoj_drain_11042026/, fixtures go_callret_discard, go_callret_keep, go_var_discard, go_blank, go_blank_var).\n\nTHE DEFECT. INV-komoj's return lift records which RESULT POSITION of a multi-value return carries a source's value, and WI-sitaf (PR #1805) made a caller's blank target at that position mean \"nothing received\". Both rest on ddg_build recording the IDENTIFIERS in each result position of a return statement. When the source call is written directly in the return, there is no identifier at that position, the position is not recorded, and taint._received_seeds takes the seed-everything fallback in the caller. The error variable is then seeded and the chain climbs exactly as WI-sitaf described.\n\nREPRO, shipped CLI, cold cache, claim host_secret -> subprocess:\n\n    func get() (string, error) { return os.Getenv(\"TOOL\"), nil }\n    func main() { _, err := get(); exec.Command(\"ls\", err.Error()).Run() }\n\nreads violated, exit 1, 2 evidence rows, source_returned_by get, analysis_method ddg, walk_verdict reached. A false positive: the environment value is discarded and err is nil.\n\nCONTROLS, same run: the variable form func get() (string, error) { v := os.Getenv(\"TOOL\"); return v, nil } with the same caller reads confirmed_with_caveats, exit 3, 0 evidence (WI-sitaf's fix holds). The direct-call form with the value KEPT (v, _ := get(); exec.Command(v).Run()) reads violated with returned_by get, which is correct. So the defect is the position of a CALL EXPRESSION in a multi-value return, nothing else.\n\nFIX SHAPE (structural, per WI-sitaf's own rule \"not a name rule on err\"): record a result position for a source CALL in a return statement, not only for an identifier -- the lift already knows the source call's line and the return's result list, so the position is the index of the result whose span contains the call. Then _received_seeds maps it like any other. Tests to carry: the repro above (must go exit 3), the kept-value control (must stay violated), and INV-komoj's test_go_multi_value_return pair.\n\nNOT MEASURED: how many corpus lifts take this fallback. The spelling (return os.Getenv(x), nil) is common Go; WI-sitaf's corpus A/B counted buildah's walks False 1 -> 21 for the variable form only."  # 7f15
    fields: {}  # 7f15
