- op: discuss  # 6342
  at: '2026-11-04T21:29:17Z'  # 6342
  by: agent  # 6342
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6342
  clock: 3  # 6342
  nonce: '6342'  # 6342
  message: "Fixed in PR #2050 (dev d1631780df). Root cause as filed: the return lift placed a value by the IDENTIFIERS per result position, and a source call written directly in the result list has none of its own (Go's Getenv is a field_identifier), so no position was recorded and the caller took the seed-everything fallback. Fix: ddg_build.ReturnStatement gains names, every name token per result position (identifiers plus field, property and scoped names), kept apart from results so the walk still matches a VARIABLE against identifiers only; taint._lift_returned_sources' direct branch places a multi-value return's call at the position whose names include the callee's short name (member_short_name of the id's name slot), a tail call still passes positions through, and mixed arities still fall back to every variable.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, shipped CLI, cold cache, claim host_secret -> subprocess, pinned in test_taint_return_flow.py (red before): the filed shape (get returns os.Getenv(\"TOOL\"), nil; main does _, err := get(); exec.Command(\"ls\", err.Error())) reads confirmed_with_caveats, 0 evidence (was violated, 2 rows via err); the value kept (v, _ := get(); exec.Command(v)) stays violated with returned_by get; the lifted hop (wrap returns get(), nil; main discards into _) reads confirmed_with_caveats. WI-sitaf's four fixtures unchanged. Unit: a ReturnStatement with names places position 0; a bare three-member span places by identifiers; a callee named in no position records None; direct returns of different arity record None. test_ddg_expression_body_returns pins names for Go, a Rust tail and a JS arrow body.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: a Python twin. x = os.getenv() beside an unrelated sink reads walk not_attempted / source_not_tracked, because defs_at is built from def-use EDGES and a seeded variable with no use has none, and with a use the walk forfeits (escaped, no reason): the Python verdict cannot show the position either way; that is the walk's standing conservatism, not this item, and no item was filed for it. Corpus delta NOT measured (the description's own \"not measured\" stands); the fix changes only which variables a caller is seeded on in this spelling, in the fewer-false-violations direction."  # 6342
